1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,040
I haven't slept a single full hour in three straight years, and my body is finally starting to shatter.

2
00:00:08,340 --> 00:00:15,708
Every single night at midnight, my eyes snap wide open. My heart races like I just ran a marathon.

3
00:00:16,008 --> 00:00:23,688
Doctors call it severe insomnia. They hand me heavy pills that do nothing except numb my daytime thoughts.

4
00:00:23,988 --> 00:00:30,996
Tonight, I set up a camera to catch whatever steals my rest. The screen reveals a terrifying truth.

5
00:00:31,296 --> 00:00:38,472
On the video, I sit up. I smile a bright, genuine smile. A smile I haven't felt in years.

6
00:00:38,772 --> 00:00:45,876
That body isn't mine. It moves with a fierce confidence, laughing softly at jokes I never heard.

7
00:00:46,176 --> 00:00:53,376
I watch myself walk straight out of the apartment, leaving my exhausted, hollow shell behind in bed.

8
00:00:53,676 --> 00:01:00,324
I follow the digital ghost through cold city streets until she enters a nursing home down the road.

9
00:01:00,624 --> 00:01:08,328
She stops by my aging mother's bedside, whispering secrets that heal the old woman's chronic nightmares.

10
00:01:08,628 --> 00:01:17,028
My sleepless nights are the exact price my mother pays to finally dream in peace. Who is sleeping while you bleed?
